# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COURSE NAVIGATION MENU  (www/menu-courses.jemdoc)
#
# Every course page (ee301.html, ee502.html, research-methods.html) includes
# THIS menu, so the sidebar inside a course lists the other courses. That is what
# makes each course feel like its own site without duplicating any page.
#
#   * The FIRST line is the site name, and it is the link to the home page.
#   * A line WITHOUT brackets is a coloured section heading.
#   * A line with brackets is a link:  Visible text [target-file.html]
#
# "All courses" goes back to the overview, which lives on the main site and uses
# the main menu (www/menu.jemdoc).
#
# To add a course: add its page in www/, add one line under "Courses" here, add
# one card to www/courses.jemdoc, and add the course to the main menu too.
#
# Careful: jemdoc marks the current entry with a SUFFIX test, so one page name
# must never be the tail of another. See guide.md §6.4.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
